  "body": "Step 7.2 of https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/timers-and-user-prompts.html#timer-initialisation-steps says \"Invoke the Function.\" but doesn't call https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#report-the-exception, i.e. `setTimeout(function(){throw new Error();})` doesn't fire global object's error events.\r\n\r\nGiven that:\r\n\r\n- `setTimeout(\"throw new Error();\");` triggers #report-the-exception (from https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#run-a-classic-script)\r\n- Browsers fire global object's error events both for `setTimeout(function)` and `setTimeout(string)` cases, as observed in https://wpt.fyi/results/html/webappapis/scripting/events/event-handler-processing-algorithm-error/window-runtime-error.html?label=experimental&label=master&aligned and https://wpt.fyi/results/workers/interfaces/WorkerGlobalScope/onerror/exception-in-onerror.html?label=experimental&label=master&aligned\r\n- Some of other callers of `Invoke` explicitly call `#report-the-exception` when `Invoke` throws.\r\n\r\n`#report-the-exception` is needed here. I'm preparing a PR.",
